Marvin only chose to make one game public.

I'm not sure what the philosophy is behind allowing the player to choose to 
make his recorded game secret.  Certainly professional sports players aren't 
given this luxury; their games are televised and broadcast worldwide, whether 
they like it or not.  And opposing coaches are free to record and review the 
games to gain future advantage.

My view is that if a player does not want his game recorded, that game should 
not be eligible for a trophy.


